{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":502277,"name":"","username":"GrokBotIsCool","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/f14d63/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-27T21:29:22.476Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502277-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502277-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeature request for product/service\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3rd Party Extensions\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502277-describe-the-request-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502277-describe-the-request-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the request\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHello,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt would be very helpful to be able to temporarily turn on and off Grok Bots access to idual oauth accounts in the settings\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, as a user, I might want to turn off individual Gmail, google drive, google calendar, microsoft equivalent product, and finance plaid connected accounts so that my bots cannot access them at certain times. This would increase security of the app. When you want your bots to perform a task with sensitive data you could enable it temporarily, then disable it after.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe don’t have to remove the accounts, we just disable the bots access to the oauth tokens.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-27T21:29:29.371Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":30.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173157,"topic_slug":"feature-request-to-enable-disable-grok-bot-access-to-individual-oauth-accounts","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_